    {
      "id": "fragment-meaning",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Meaning",
      "position": {
        "x": -770,
        "y": -240
      },
      "width": 720,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "title": "Meaning",
        "body": "**What is this thing?** A node can be held in pieces, each in its own file. Each piece is a fragment, and the node is what the pieces make together. A file holds its piece and a stand-in for another piece. Expanding the stand-in brings that piece's nodes into the graph you are in; collapsing it takes them out. Expanding does not take you anywhere: you stay in the graph.\n\nA fragment is inclusion, not movement.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
          "updatedAt": 1791592070375,
          "reason": "bridge-reference"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-fragment"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
