    {
      "id": "fragment-contract",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Contract",
      "position": {
        "x": 910,
        "y": -240
      },
      "width": 720,
      "height": 380,
      "data": {
        "title": "Contract",
        "body": "- *Stand-in:* a `fragment` node whose `data.target` has `mode: \"expand\"` and a `ref` to the other piece. Like a Portal it draws a face of what it stands for (`sourcePayload`, `surfaceId`).\n- *Optional pin:* `target.expectedHash` makes the host accept only that exact version of the piece.\n- *Limits:* a piece brings at most 200 nodes and 400 edges.\n- *Policy:* the host's trust policy decides which protocols, repositories and hosts a piece may come from.\n- *Code and Bridges:* a Method, Script, Import or Export in a piece is withheld unless the host's stand-in allows it. `target.allow` lists a type (every one of that type) or a type with an address (`{ type: 'import', ref }`, only a Bridge to that graph). The grant is read from the stand-in in the host, never from the piece or from whoever asks.\n- *Ids:* included nodes get ids of the host graph (`exp_…:canonicalId`). Each records what it was in its piece (`data._origin.canonicalId`) and arrives tagged `untrusted` (`data._expansion`).",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "bridge",
          "updatedAt": 1791592070379,
          "reason": "bridge-reference"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-fragment"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
